    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_Recovery_SectionTitle">Recovery</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_RevertTitle">Revert to Windows Defaults</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_RevertDesc">Undo system optimizations and return your PC to its previous state using Windows System Restore.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_RevertButton">Restore System</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_RevertDialogTitle">Revert to Defaults?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_RevertDialogContent">EvolveOS Optimizer uses Windows System Restore to safely revert all changes made to your system.&#x0a;&#x0a;Clicking 'Continue' will open the Windows System Restore wizard. Please select the restore point named 'EvolveOS Initial Backup' to undo all tweaks.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_RevertMissingTitle">Restore Point Missing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_RevertMissingContent">The 'EvolveOS Optimizer Initial Backup' restore point could not be found. You may have opted out of creating it, or Windows automatically deleted it to free up disk space.&#x0a;&#x0a;You can still continue to open the System Restore wizard to look for older, manual restore points.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_ShowRestorePointOnStart">Prompt to create a restore point on startup</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_ShowRestorePointOnStartDesc">Shows a prompt to create a system restore point every time you launch the application.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_RestoreTweaksTitle">Restore Optimizer Tweaks</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_RestoreTweaksDesc">Safely revert all settings modified by EvolveOS Optimizer back to their initial state when you first launched the app.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_RestoreTweaksButton">Restore Tweaks</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_ForceWindowsDefaultsTitle">Force Windows Defaults</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_ForceWindowsDefaultsDesc">Wipe out all custom settings and force the system back to standard Microsoft defaults. Useful if you used a custom ISO or debloat script before installing EvolveOS Optimizer.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_ForceWindowsDefaultsButton">Factory Reset</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_RestoreTweaksDialogTitle">Restore Optimizer Tweaks?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_RestoreTweaksDialogContent">This will safely revert all settings modified by EvolveOS Optimizer back to the exact state they were in when you first launched the app.&#x0a;&#x0a;Are you sure you want to continue?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_ForceWindowsDefaultsDialogTitle">Force Windows Defaults?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_ForceWindowsDefaultsDialogContent">This will wipe out all custom settings managed by the optimizer and force your system back to standard Microsoft factory defaults.&#x0a;&#x0a;This is highly recommended if you used a custom ISO or debloat script before installing EvolveOS.&#x0a;&#x0a;Are you sure you want to continue?</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_ResetAppTitle">Reset App Preferences</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_ResetAppDesc">Restore all EvolveOS Optimizer settings (themes, dashboard layout, languages) back to their default values.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_ResetAppButton">Reset App</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_ResetAppWarning">Note: This only affects the application's interface and behavior. It will not undo your Windows system tweaks.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_ResetAppDialogTitle">Reset App Preferences?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings_ResetAppDialogContent">This will reset all EvolveOS Optimizer preferences (themes, dashboard layout, auto-optimization thresholds, etc.) back to their defaults.&#x0a;&#x0a;This will NOT revert your Windows tweaks.&#x0a;&#x0a;Continue?</sys:String>

