    <sys:String x:Key="tgl6_intf">Taskbar transparency effect</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl7_intf">Dark Taskbar theme</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl8_intf">Dark theme of applications and explorer</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl9_intf">Delay when calling the context menu</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl10_intf">Delay in the appearance of previews on the taskbar</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl11_intf">Arrows for shortcuts to files, folders, or programs</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl12_intf">Prefix «Label for...»/ postfix «– Label»</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl13_intf">«This PC» icon on Desktop</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl14_intf">«Trash» icon on Desktop</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl15_intf">Taskbar Alignment</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl16_intf">Standard layout of the «Start» menu</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl17_intf">Stripped-down context menu</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl18_intf">Show tips and suggestions</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl19_intf">Use Compact Explorer mode</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl20_intf">«Copilot» and «Recall» Assistants</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl21_intf">«End task» RMB on the application</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl22_intf">Show window snap assist layouts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl23_intf">Icons and buttons on the taskbar</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl24_intf">Show personalized ads</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl25_intf">Restore previous folder windows when logging in</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl26_intf">Notifications with Windows tips and suggestions</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl27_intf">Folders located in «This PC»</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl28_intf">«3D Objects» in the explorer</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl29_intf">Compression of wallpaper format .JPEG of the desktop</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl30_intf">Tooltips for desktop elements</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl31_intf">Search query with «Bing» integration in Start menu</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl32_intf">Open «Quick Access» instead of «This PC»</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl33_intf">Displaying file extensions in explorer</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl34_intf">Disable acrylic blur effect on the login screen</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl35_intf">Gallery in the navigation pane of File Explorer</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl36_intf">Home in the navigation pane of File Explorer</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl37_intf">Duplicate removable drives from navigation pane of File Explorer</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl38_intf">Displaying hidden files and folders in explorer</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl39_intf">Snap bar (Windows 11)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl40_intf">Show seconds in taskbar clock</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="tgl1_desc_intf">Will change the color of the cursor selection from blue to gray «wet asphalt».</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl2_desc_intf">Will change the color of the tooltip in some programs from yellow to light blue «azure».</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl3_desc_intf">A tweak reduces the size of the Minimize, Maximize, and Close buttons, making them less bulky. It adjusts the size for all windows, including File Explorer, Photos, browsers, and other familiar programs.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl4_desc_intf">A tweak increases the frequency of the text cursor's blinking. By default, the cursor blinks every 530 milliseconds.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl5_desc_intf">A tweak reduces the thickness of scrollbars in classic Windows applications, including File Explorer, browsers, and other legacy programs. However, it does not affect modern interfaces, as they utilize their own control elements independent of system settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl6_desc_intf">Tweak will disable or enable the transparency effect. Translucent windows and surfaces.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl7_desc_intf">Changes the taskbar theme to light or dark. Attention, the screen may blink.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl8_desc_intf">The tweak will change the explorer theme to light or dark, including browsers and other programs that support the device theme. Attention the screen may blink.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl9_desc_intf">By default, additional context menu items appear with a delay of 400 milliseconds. If you want to go faster, you can reduce this delay.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl10_desc_intf">By default, the Taskbar preview shows previews of running applications for too long. To make previews appear faster, apply this tweak.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl11_desc_intf">Tweak will remove arrows from labels by replacing the arrow file.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl12_desc_intf">Removing the too intuitive prefix-postfix for labels.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl13_desc_intf">The PC icon, unlike the PC shortcut, is better because it has the necessary properties of the context menu and is free of unnecessary ones.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl14_desc_intf">If you do not need the Trash icon on the desktop and you do not want to waste time looking for a shutdown, then you can use tweaks.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl15_desc_intf">Choose where you want the icons on the taskbar to be displayed, on the cent or on the left</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl16_desc_intf">Changes the Start menu layout by expanding the area for pinned apps. In addition, except in the Windows Home edition, the «Recommended» section will be removed from the Start menu.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl17_desc_intf">This tweak will return you to the usual classic context menu for the desktop and «Explorer». Attention the screen may blink.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl18_desc_intf">Windows 11 sometimes shows hints on how to use a particular feature, for example, the new «Start» menu or «Quick Settings». They are useful if you are seeing Windows 11 for the first time, as it is useless junk.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl19_desc_intf">By default, Windows adds padding between items in Explorer. This is a new feature designed for touch screens. This tweak will restore the classic layout of the file explorer, removing the indentation between the elements and saving you from searching for settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl20_desc_intf">The tweak disables and, where possible, hides Copilot icons on the taskbar, in the «Start Menu», in Edge, and in Notepad, blocking its functionality, and also disables Recall. At the same time, the core Copilot application itself is not affected, remains in the system, and can be used if needed. Copilot can only be fully removed along with Microsoft Edge. If these AI features are not present in your Windows initially, using the tweak is pointless.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl21_desc_intf">This tweak will allow you to add the «End task» option to the context menu when you right-click on the application on the taskbar. This speeds up the completion of processes without having to open the task Manager. Attention the screen may blink.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl22_desc_intf">If you don’t need to see the snap layout suggestions when hovering over the «Maximize» button, you can disable this option.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl23_desc_intf">This tweak removes the «Search», «Task View», and «Chat» icons, and hides the «Learn about this picture» element. On older builds of Windows 11, it also removes the Copilot icon. For Windows 10 users, it additionally disables «News and Interests» and Cortana. Attention the screen may blink.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl24_desc_intf">By default, Windows uses the collected information to target ads, i.e. to display ads that match your interests. And literally, this advertisement is located wherever free space is available for display. If you don't want Windows to display personalized ads in all Store apps, Explorer, Options, and the Start menu, then you can disable this junk.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl25_desc_intf">By default, Windows does not save the positions of windows, as well as their state when turned off. This tweak will allow you to remember the type of open folders in order to restore them after Logging out, Rebooting and Shutting down.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl26_desc_intf">Tweak allows disabling all Windows tips and notifications, including online hints in settings, as well as disabling Second Chance Out of Box Experience (SCOOBE) for Windows 11 users. SCOOBE is suddenly appearing pop-up that aggressively prompts user to «complete device setup urgently» and sign in to Microsoft account.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl27_desc_intf">Tweak will hide folders from «This PC»: Desktop, Videos, Documents, Downloads, Images, Music. Attention the screen may blink.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl28_desc_intf">Removes the 3D Objects item from the Explorer Overview in the left menu list (from the Explorer list tree). Attention the screen may blink.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl29_desc_intf">By default, when you set a jpeg image as your desktop wallpaper, Windows automatically reduces its quality to 85%. This tweak will set the jpeg wallpaper quality to 100%.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl30_desc_intf">Tweak will disable tooltips for desktop elements when hovering the mouse cursor.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl31_desc_intf">By default, Windows sends everything you search for in the «Start» menu to its servers to provide you with Bing search results. If you don't need Bing integration in the «Start» menu, you can apply a tweak to disable web search. Attention the screen may blink.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl32_desc_intf">By default, when you open Explorer, the first tab will be «Quick Access». And to open any disk, you need to make unnecessary movements. This tweak will make «This PC» open when opened, rather than «Quick Access».</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl33_desc_intf">By default, Windows hides file extensions, which makes the File Explorer view less cluttered. If needed, you can enable the display of file extensions using this tweak, saving you the time spent searching. Attention the screen may blink.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl34_desc_intf">By default, the sign-in screen background image has an acrylic blur effect as part of Windows 11 transparency effects.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl35_desc_intf">Show or hide Gallery in the navigation pane of File Explorer.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl36_desc_intf">Show or hide Home in the navigation pane of File Explorer.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl37_desc_intf">By default, You may find that when connecting a removable drive to the computer, the drive displays twice in File Explorer. This tweak allows you to hide the duplicate removable drives from navigation pane of File Explorer.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl38_desc_intf">By default, Windows hides files and folders. Users may want to access hidden files to customize their system preferences, such as modifying system themes, icons, or startup settings. Hidden folders like “AppData” contain user-specific application data and settings, allowing users to tailor their Windows 11 experience to their preferences.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl39_desc_intf">By default in Windows 11, The snap bar appears when you drag a window to the top of the screen. The tweak allow you to disable the snap bar.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl40_desc_intf">Choose if you want seconds in the taskbar clock to show, windows by default doesn't show the seconds in the taskbar clock.</sys:String>
    <!-- endregion Interface Page-->

    <!-- region Privacy Page -->
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl1_conf">Advertising identifier and targeted advertising</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl2_conf">All types of syncing your data</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl3_conf">Collection and monitoring of Windows telemetry</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl4_conf">Collecting data through scheduler events</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl5_conf">Collecting data about installed applications</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl6_conf">Collecting application usage statistics</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl7_conf">Collecting and sending handwriting data</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl8_conf">Collecting hardware configuration data</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl9_conf">Network access to spy Microsoft domains</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl10_conf">Determining the user's location</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl11_conf">Checking requests through Feedback</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl12_conf">Hidden background updates of speech synthesis</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl13_conf">Hidden monitoring of your system</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl14_conf">Hidden experiments on your system</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl15_conf">Services for covert data collection and transmission</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl16_conf">«Logging» Windows Events</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl17_conf">Collection and monitoring of NVIDIA telemetry</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl18_conf">Keeping a record of user behavior</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl19_conf">Collecting data and background updates of Offline maps</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl20_conf">Collection and monitoring of Intel telemetry</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="tgl1_desc_conf">Windows creates a unique advertising identifier for each user to track your actions. Which is used by application developers and Windows itself for their own purposes, including to offer you specific ads in applications.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl2_desc_conf">Even using a local account, Windows always tries to synchronize your data with Microsoft servers. In particular, the following: themes, passwords, Windows settings, browser settings, language bar settings, simplified access settings, additional settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl3_desc_conf">Telemetry (diagnostic data) is data that Windows automatically collects to send to Microsoft servers, or in short, "What? Where?  Why and when do you use it?". Microsoft claims that the data is depersonalized and helps the company develop Windows. Even if you are not concerned about the fact of collecting information, then another problem may arise - excessive load on the processor, which in turn slows down the system.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl4_desc_conf">In the «Task Scheduler» there are services that, after their work, collect data about their work and send it to the Microsoft server.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl5_desc_conf">Microsoft collects data about your software. This information is used by Microsoft to diagnose compatibility issues, but you will not help Microsoft improve compatibility in new versions of Windows because this information is used only for selfish purposes for Microsoft. Disabling this feature prevents potentially sensitive information from being sent.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl6_desc_conf">The tweak will disable the application usage monitoring function, eliminating the collection of data on usage frequency, work duration, and other productivity metrics. As a result, the system will stop analyzing your work process, ensuring the protection of your confidential information.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl7_desc_conf">This tweak disables the data collection mechanism that Microsoft uses to improve its handwriting recognition technology. Regardless of whether you use this feature or not, the system was tracking your activity to enhance recognition accuracy. The changes implemented prevent such data collection, helping to preserve privacy.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl8_desc_conf">The Software Quality Improvement Program (CEIP) is a separate feature that collects information about the configuration of your hardware and how you use the software and services. The program also periodically downloads a file to collect information about problems that you may have with Windows. The program is voluntary and you do not have to send your data to Microsoft, violating your privacy.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl9_desc_conf">This tweak modifies the hosts file by adding the address 0.0.0.0 before specific domain names, effectively blocking them. Additionally, it adjusts the Windows firewall settings to block connections to several IP addresses associated with Microsoft's data collection services.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl10_desc_conf">Disabling geolocation services significantly reduces the potential for using location data for advertising purposes – access to this information is restricted not only for Microsoft services but also for any third-party applications and scripts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl11_desc_conf">The tweak blocks the collection of feedback and its notifications in Windows, which prevents data from being transmitted without your consent. Meanwhile, even if you do not use the «Feedback» feature, Microsoft still logs how frequently you contact official support.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl12_desc_conf">Windows is capable of recognizing speech using a dedicated speech recognition and synthesis module. Even if you do not use Cortana or «Ease of Access», your operating system by default always checks for updates to its voice recognition engine.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl13_desc_conf">A function that has access to any user data. It exchanges some information with Microsoft servers and does not affect the operation of the operating system or applications in any way. It does not help the user in any way, which makes it useless.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl14_desc_conf">Microsoft regularly conducts experiments with Windows users to determine whether a feature is widely used, whether changing a feature makes it more useful. But in turn, this is a violation of confidentiality.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl15_desc_conf">The services DiagTrack, dmwappushservice, and diagsvc act as keyloggers — they record every user activity, including keystrokes, and send this data to Microsoft's servers without the user's consent. When using UWF (Unified Write Filter), the stable operation of the system depends on the dmwappushservice service. However, if you do not know what it is or if you have an alternative tool, it makes sense to get rid of these keyloggers.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl16_desc_conf">An event log that collects and processes system diagnostic information, wasting your computer's resources. The service will not give you anything good, it is better to disable it, so you will prevent the sending of confidential information.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl17_desc_conf">The service that is responsible for collecting and transmitting data about the system and its use, or a function that is not related to the operation of the video driver, is useless. Why and what kind of information NVIDIA collects is known only to itself. But the fact that this does not bring anything useful to the end user is quite obvious.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl18_desc_conf">The tweak disables the UAR (User Activity Recording) feature – a system that sequentially logs every action you take on your computer: from taking screenshots and typing text to launching programs and even providing access to the webcam while the screen is locked, and much more.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl19_desc_conf">Windows periodically updates Offline maps and sends notifications about new data in the background. These processes may collect information about your location, routes, and map usage. If you do not use Offline maps, it is recommended to disable them to avoid hidden updates and data transmission to Microsoft servers without your direct involvement.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="tgl20_desc_conf">The Intel module, which operates in the background to collect and transmit data, is positioned as a tool for improving the company’s products. However, for the average user it provides little practical benefit, and disabling this feature can reduce background activity and prevent unnecessary data transmission.</sys:String>
    <!-- endregion Privacy Page -->

