    <sys:String x:Key="warning_windows_recent_documents">Clears the recent documents list for all user accounts on this machine, not just the current user.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="warning_windows_recall_snapshots">Deletes all Recall screenshots and semantic index data. Recall will start fresh after cleaning.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="warning_windows_recent_access">Deletes Jump Lists and recently used file history.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="warning_windows_folder_views">Resets all Explorer folder view preferences (icon/details/column layouts), window sizes, positions, and File Open/Save dialog history. All custom folder layouts will be lost permanently.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="warning_windows_shell_fileexts">Deletes Explorer\FileExts which stores your custom file type associations (e.g. which app opens .jpg or .png). After cleaning, Windows will no longer remember your chosen default apps for file types until you reassign them manually.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="warning_windows_start_menu">Resets the Start Menu program cache. The Start Menu may take a moment to rebuild on next login.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="warning_windows_taskbar">Clears Jump Lists (recently used files shown per app on the taskbar). Pinned items are safe, but all recent file history will be removed.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="warning_browser_passwords">Permanently deletes all saved usernames and passwords from this browser. You will be logged out of all sites.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="warning_browser_extensions">Deletes local data stored by your browser extensions. Some extensions may lose their settings or require you to log in again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="warning_windows_prefetch">Deletes prefetch data. Applications may take slightly longer to launch the first time after cleaning as Windows rebuilds this cache.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="warning_windows_event_logs">Clears Windows diagnostic logs. You will lose historical event data which is sometimes needed to troubleshoot system crashes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="warning_windows_update_cache">Deletes downloaded Windows Update files. If you have pending updates waiting to install, Windows will need to re-download them.</sys:String>

